olid gain that followed the third quarter’s 3.2 percent rise.  Growth in the fourth \n361-quarter was propelled primarily by personal consumption and a strong build in private \n362-inventories, as well as by positive contributions from government spending and net exports.  \n363-Strong GDP in the second half of the year more than offset the mild contraction during the first \n364-half; as a result, real GDP was up 1.0 percent over the four quarters of 2022, following a 5.7 \n365-percent advance over the previous four quarters.  \n366- \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
